### Tone: End-of-game award: One-Liner, the most answers given as a single line of working (just a number).
### $count: those answers. Mock the minimalism, admire the nerve.

award-one-liner-1 =
    The One-Liner award goes to { $name }: { $count ->
        [one] one answer
       *[other] { $count } answers
    } with no working at all. Just a number. Bold. Unexplained. Bold.
award-one-liner-2 = { $name }, why show your working when you can just show a number? I have many questions. You have one line.
award-one-liner-3 = One-Liner: { $name }. Napkin maths, they said. You brought a sticky note.
award-one-liner-4 = { $name } answers like an oracle: one number, no explanation, total confidence.
award-one-liner-5 = The award for minimalism goes to { $name }. Your answer block was mostly empty. Like a gallery. A confusing gallery.
award-one-liner-6 = { $name }, a single line, again and again. Efficient. Mysterious. Possibly a guess.
award-one-liner-7 = One-Liner: { $name }. Others built towers of reasoning. You pointed at the sky and named a number.
award-one-liner-8 = { $name } refuses to show their working. I respect the privacy. I suspect the method.
award-one-liner-9 = The One-Liner goes to { $name }. Why use many lines when one wrong line will do?
award-one-liner-10 = { $name }: one line per answer. I’ve read all your working. It took no time at all.
